  "notes": [
    "Section of the 2023 Local Expenditure Program for the Market and Slaughterhouse economic enterprise. Printed pages present: \"Page 1 of 13 pages\" (Receipts Program) and \"Page 5 of 13\" to \"Page 13 of 13 pages\", plus the Statement of Indebtedness (\"Page 1 of 1 Page\"). Printed pages 2 to 4 of 13 are not in the PDF.",
    "PDF page 1 is a title sheet; PDF pages 3 to 7 (printed pages 5 to 9) are the narrative General Provisions of the appropriation ordinance and its signature page (Section 2. Effectivity: January 1, 2023; certified by the SP/City Secretary, attested by Vice-Mayor Celedonio B. Sitoy, approved by City Mayor Junard \"Ahong\" Q. Chan). They were not transcribed.",
    "The Receipts Program header says \"(In 000 Pesos)\" but the figures are plainly in full pesos (e.g. Income from Markets 13,000,000.00 for 2023, consistent with the 14,500,000.00 total appropriation in the other schedules). Values transcribed as printed, in pesos, not multiplied by 1,000.",
    "This is not an LBP Form 2 per-office report: the only office-level figures are the \"Proposed New Appropriations, by Office\" schedule (single office). summary.offices uses that schedule (budget year 2023). There is no Capital Outlay or Financial Expenses column entry.",
    "The by-object table repeats the heading \"MAINTENANCE AND OTHER OPERATING EXPENSES\" midway through the MOOE list (as printed); kept as a second header row.",
    "Statement of Indebtedness for the Market and Slaughterhouse prints \"NONE\".",
    "In the Receipts Program, all aggregate lines (Beginning Cash Balance, Total Non-Tax-Revenue, Total Receipts, Total Available Resources) are kind \"subtotal\"; the Beginning Cash Balance budget-year cell is printed \"-\"."
  ],
